# Putting things in Russian: поставь, положи, повесь
subtitle: "Unpacking in Tom's new flat: поста́вь, положи́ or пове́сь for upright, flat or hanging, на сте́ну for where to, and над, под, ме́жду for where."
tags: ["russian","поставить положить","put in russian","russian verbs","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/placing-verbs","grammar/prepositions","vocabulary/moving-house"]
thumb: "band \"Stand it, lay it or hang it?\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Formal Russian: ты, вы and Нина Петровна","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/105-russian-formal-you.cast"}

